From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: surfaces

IDCompositionDevice::CreateSurface and CreateVirtualSurface (E_NOTIMPL
until now) make a surface: a Direct3D 11 texture on the device the
DirectComposition device was made for (or one of its own when that is
NULL), 1 to 16384 pixels each way, B8G8R8A8, R8G8B8A8 or R16G16B16A16_FLOAT
with premultiplied or ignored alpha; other arguments are E_INVALIDARG.
BeginDraw hands out the texture as the interface asked for with the offset
of the update rectangle (a rectangle outside the surface is E_INVALIDARG),
EndDraw takes it back; Suspend/ResumeDraw, and the errors
DCOMPOSITION_ERROR_SURFACE_BEING_RENDERED / _NOT_BEING_RENDERED for calls in
the wrong state. Scroll moves the pixels of a rectangle, writing only inside
the clip rectangle; a virtual surface can be resized (the pixels that stay
are kept) and trimmed. A visual whose content is a surface shows it: on
Commit the changed texture is copied to the back buffer of a composition
swap chain the surface keeps for the purpose and presented, which the device
already shows in the window.
